  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1229 PM MDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nThe monsoon moisture plume is forecast to continue to produce \ndaily rounds of scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms \nmainly over central and western parts of the forecast area \nSaturday through Tuesday as the upper high varies its position \neast of NM and the upper low on the OR coast gradually sweeps \ninland over the northern Rockies. There will be a continued risk \nof locally heavy rainfall and flash flooding Saturday through at \nleast Monday as anomalously high PWATs continue to vary around \n1-1.3 inches. The steering flow will also slow down this weekend \nas the upper high aloft draws closer to NM. Models vary on whether\nthe upper low over the northern Rockies will begin to steer drier\nair over NM on Tuesday, potentially resulting in a downtick in \nstorm coverage and rainfall intensity at least over northwest \nparts of the state. Models vary even more on the position of the \nupper high after Tuesday, with drier solutions indicating a \ncentroid near or just north of NM, and wetter solutions \nrecentering the upper high over the Mississippi River.",
